  "note": "Borough election, 18 May 1949: twelve councillors, four for each ward (the three aldermen retired in 1952). Only the Town Hall Ward went to the poll, five candidates for four seats. The Market Ward members, four nominees for four seats, are named from the nomination report (Ballymena Weekly Telegraph, 6 May 1949, p. 5). Harryville Ward had five nominations for its four seats but was not polled; who withdrew is not found, so its members are not recorded (Irish News, 20 May 1949, p. 3). Electorate 1,697; 960 voted; three spoiled papers. Mr. Murphy, a former Mayor and member for 29 years, was the only Catholic member and lost his seat."
